Z||000006||Digisys||09-25-2001||02:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87GTZ34:<BR><B>Digisys, No harm done I figured you were new & thought I'd give the tip.  People won't ignore you for being new but sometimes it seems that people are all offline at once.  It sounds like your positioning logic makes sense for TDC.  Did you see my response on the original post?<P><FONT COLOR="blue">Yes, I did see the response and take it that you are saying compression is not all that important at this stage. I had the motor<BR>totally together Sun. with the valves set at 1 1/2 turns. As I tried to crank it up, it just didn't sound right. Sounded like it was spinning over really fast, don't know if this is normal because my car has always started right up. Plus all it did was pop back a couple of times. So I pulled it back down to remove valve covers. Thought I might have gone to far on the adjustment and the valves maybe where not seating entirely !<BR> Anyway, I guess I will reset them to 1 1/2 put everything back together and try again !!<BR>PS. Everything is stock. Thanks for the help !!!</FONT><P><BR>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 09-25-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||7
