Z||000009||87GTZ34||09-25-2001||10:14 PM||||Digisys,  You are right about the lack of compression if you've been cranking it already and the valves are not seating with 1&1/2 turns then something is amiss.  I can assure you though if you have stock lifters, push rods, springs and rockers that 1&1/2 should work.  Is it possible that as you were turning the rocker nut down, you didn't catch the zero lash point.  Just asking here but that would give the symptom that you're describing.  With a lifter that has little/no oil in it, feeling the 'bottom out' of the push rod is very sensitive. (and they say guys aren't sensitive...   You shouldn't feel the psuh rod 'bind' up but should feel no space before touching 'something' in this case the lifter.  Also, when wiggling the pushrod checking for zero lash, you shouldn't apply much pressure at all in order to feel the exact point of zero lash.  If this is all 'old news', my apologies just trying to get you going.  I know what no Fiero withdrawl is like.  GL If you want to talk with me, then send an email (email in profile) and I'll send my phone # or call you if you send yours.  GL<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 09-26-2001).]||||reg||1
